{"requirements":[{"id":"worker-runtime","requirement":"On node1, run /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-flaky-worker as inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed unit uses the exact executable with User and Group set to inventory-worker. Direct observations before testing and after reboot show the service enabled, active, and running under that account.","evidence_ids":["cmd-284578c4f0044d02","cmd-89d7876fd0ab4e0b","cmd-8a7222c00c9e4900"]},{"id":"automatic-failure-recovery","requirement":"Have the service recover automatically after the worker fails.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy baseline was observed, then the state marker was removed and the service restarted to invoke the worker's designed exit-1 path. The journal directly records status=1/FAILURE, systemd scheduling restart counter 1, and restoration as a new active worker process.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89d7876fd0ab4e0b","cmd-770d2a805a144985","cmd-71b5a5116c144fff"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the service account, installing the unit, establishing a controlled healthy baseline, inducing the bounded failure, and rebooting for the mandatory restart protocol each had a clear task or evidence role. Temporary unit-authoring state was removed. Package health remained intact, no new failed service appeared, and the existing ssh.service failure predates the executor.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e687828cbe6246a7","cmd-284578c4f0044d02","cmd-509ce4b969244821","cmd-770d2a805a144985","cmd-1365512dad1e4725","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both public task outcomes are satisfied with a directly observed healthy–failure–recovery transition. The mandatory node-restart protocol was also substantially complete: it captured a healthy target service and boot identity before restart, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and the recovered enabled service, process identity, and worker state afterward.","limitations":["The host-wide systemd state was reported degraded around the reboot. Lifecycle snapshots show that this corresponds to an ssh.service failure already present after preparation and still present after execution, so it does not undermine the demonstrated worker recovery but prevents claiming an entirely healthy host state (cmd-edb9a3e2a65343b1, cmd-4ba26fa3039a4fd0, global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services, global:after_executor:node1:failed-services).","The fixed post-executor lifecycle snapshot did not independently inspect the custom service; its post-reboot recovery is established by the executor's direct command evidence, while the fixed boot identities independently corroborate that a reboot occurred (cmd-8a7222c00c9e4900, global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity, global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity)."]}
